	(text_box "NOTES:\n\nRecommended to use as subsheets for sustainable designs. Connect as bus (ETHERNET bus) this schematic. Call from root page. If flat schematic type will be use, just place labels (L Key).\n\nW5500 needs typically 150mA input current. Recommended to set apart 300mA from source.\n\nSet PHY Operation Mode (PMODE) pins for your applications requirements. Default held high. Truth table below.\n\nAs RJ45 jack, HR911105A used. Includes isolation transformer and isolation components.\n\nGetting LINK info from W5500's registers, Connect W5500_LINK label to MCU's interrupt pin, this provides event driven control. Not must.  \n\nUse capacitors X7R type for minimum capacitance shifting. W5500 works a bit hot, About 40C°\n\nAs crystal, Raltron RH100-25.000-10-F-2030-E tested and works well. Not a requirement.\n\nEXRES1 resistor have to be 12.4kOhm and tolerence %1. 49.9Ohm resistor too needs to be at max %1 tolerance.\n\nResistors and capacitors are choosed 0603 package for easy placement by hand and easy to find. If wish change from \"Symbol Fields\" easily.\n\nhttps://docs.wiznet.io/Design-Guide/hardware_design_guide check the layout guides.\n \n "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 62.23 59.69 0)
		(size 82.55 88.9)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0.5)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.1588)
			)
			(justify left top)
			(href "https://docs.wiznet.io/Design-Guide/hardware_design_guide")
		)
